{
  "catalogues": {
    "layout": {
      "literals": [
        "Direction",
        "Column is the default here, not row.",
        "flexDirection: row",
        "Three boxes left to right.",
        "flexDirection: column",
        "The default. Nothing has to ask for it.",
        "row-reverse",
        "Order flips, and so does which edge flex-start means.",
        "Main axis",
        "justifyContent, along the direction.",
        "space-between",
        "space-around",
        "center",
        "Cross axis",
        "alignItems, across the direction.",
        "stretch",
        "The default: children fill the cross axis unless they say otherwise.",
        "center",
        "flex-end",
        "alignSelf overrides it",
        "The middle box opts out of the row's alignItems.",
        "Growing and shrinking",
        "flex: 1 shares the space",
        "Each takes an equal share of what is left.",
        "Different flex values",
        "Two to one: the first takes twice the remaining space.",
        "flexShrink is 0 here, not 1",
        "The web shrinks by default and this does not, so a row of wide children overflows rather than squeezing. The second row asks to shrink.",
        "Wrapping and gaps",
        "flexWrap: wrap",
        "rowGap and columnGap",
        "Different spacing on each axis, with no margins involved.",
        "Out of flow",
        "position: absolute",
        "Positioned against the nearest parent, which here is the grey stage.",
        "Inset shorthand",
        "All four edges at once: the child fills its parent with a margin.",
        "zIndex",
        "The magenta box is written first and still paints on top.",
        "Sizing",
        "aspectRatio",
        "A width and a ratio; the height follows. Useful where an image's size is not known.",
        "Percentages",
        "Resolved during native layout, against the parent.",
        "min and max",
        "The box wants 500 wide and is capped, then floored by minHeight.",
        "Overflow",
        "overflow: hidden",
        "The child is larger than the parent and is clipped, including the rounded corner."
      ],
      "stages": 22
    },
    "typography": {
      "literals": [
        "Size and weight",
        "A type scale",
        "Weights",
        "Native maps these onto the family's real cuts; a family with no medium cut will round to the nearest it has.",
        "Italic",
        "Spacing",
        "lineHeight",
        "Left is default, right is 30. Compare the gap between wrapped lines.",
        "letterSpacing",
        "Alignment and truncation",
        "textAlign",
        "numberOfLines",
        "Truncation happens in native layout, so the ellipsis lands where the platform would put it rather than where a JavaScript guess would.",
        "ellipsizeMode: head",
        "Decoration and transform",
        "textDecorationLine",
        "textTransform",
        "Applied by the platform, so it follows the locale's casing rules rather than JavaScript's.",
        "Nesting",
        "Text inside text inherits and continues the same line.",
        "Inherited style",
        "The inner spans keep the outer size and only change what they name.",
        "A view cannot be text",
        "The pill is a view inside text, which native lays out as an inline block. It does not inherit the font.",
        "Selection and interaction",
        "selectable",
        "Long-press to select. Off by default, because on native it changes what a long-press means.",
        "A tap handler on text"
      ],
      "stages": 14
    },
    "surfaces": {
      "literals": [
        "Borders",
        "Width, colour, style",
        "One edge at a time",
        "Per-side widths and colours, which is how a divider or a leading accent is drawn.",
        "A hairline",
        "The thinnest line the screen can draw. Beside the 1px rule below it, it should be visibly finer on a 2x or 3x screen.",
        "Corners",
        "borderRadius",
        "Per-corner",
        "The four corners take different radii, which is how a sheet or a chat bubble is shaped.",
        "Depth",
        "Shadow",
        "iOS draws the offset, radius and opacity; Android maps it onto an elevation, so the two are close rather than identical.",
        "opacity",
        "Applies to the whole subtree, including text inside it.",
        "Transforms",
        "Drawn transformed; the layout is unchanged.",
        "rotate",
        "scale",
        "translate",
        "The gap it leaves is the space it still occupies in the layout.",
        "Order matters",
        "Rotate-then-translate and translate-then-rotate land in different places.",
        "Backgrounds",
        "A gradient",
        "Compiled from CSS into the structure Fabric expects, not a library.",
        "A tinted overlay",
        "A translucent view over content, which is the ordinary way to dim something.",
        "Feedback",
        "Pressed state",
        "A press changes the style through a signal; there is no CSS :active on a native view."
      ],
      "stages": 14
    },
    "css-engine": {
      "literals": [
        "Units",
        "px and rem",
        "rem is 16px, the web default. Native has no root font size to read, so one is chosen rather than guessed at.",
        "Percentages",
        "Resolved during native layout against the parent, not at build time.",
        "Viewport units",
        "vw and vh are the window, and they follow it: rotate the simulator and these change without anything re-rendering.",
        "em, against the font size in scope",
        "The inner box is 2em of the text around it, so it grows with the paragraph rather than with the root.",
        "Custom properties",
        "A token, and a rule that beats it",
        "Both boxes read --brand. The second also carries a more specific rule, which has to win - a token is resolved late, and late is not the same as important.",
        "Arithmetic around one",
        "calc() and max() over a token are folded at build time into a scale, an offset and a floor, so the device never sees an expression.",
        "Media queries",
        "prefers-color-scheme",
        "Switch the simulator between light and dark: this repaints with no code involved, because the engine re-resolves the cascade when the condition changes.",
        "width",
        "Rotate the device. The engine keeps the conditions in step through watchConditions, which an app calls once next to mount.",
        "Motion",
        "transition",
        "The property is eased on the JS thread and committed per frame. Tap to move it; tap again mid-flight and it carries on from where it had got to rather than snapping back.",
        "@keyframes",
        "A named animation, running on repeat. Compiled to the same commits a transition makes, so nothing here is a native animation driver.",
        "Inheritance",
        "What crosses a boundary and what does not",
        "Colour and font size inherit down through views to the text inside them; a border does not, because native has no notion of inheriting one."
      ],
      "stages": 11
    }
  },
